  "description": "QUZFAW crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group I 2/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C33 H51 F21 Gd4 N3 O25 1+,2(C4 H8 O1),C2 F3 O2 1-. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.813-3.924 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.53-111.99°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4(μ3-OH)4(μ-TFA)6(η1-TFA)(η3-mdeaH2)3(THF)](TFA)·2THF. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
